course: dictionary
lesson: 8368
title: Almost round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Roundish is made from round and the ending -ish, which means a bit or roughly. So roundish means almost round, but not a perfect circle or ball. «Animal cells, like the soft roundish cells scraped from your cheek, have a thin skin called a membrane instead of a stiff wall.» The cells are not perfect circles, but they are close enough to round that the writer calls them roundish.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Soft» and «scraped from your cheek» tell you the cells are small and not stiff, and «roundish» tells you their shape is near to round without being exact. Ask yourself: would «round» fit here? If it would, but the thing is not quite a perfect circle, then «roundish» is the better word.
explain: The ending -ish appears in many words. «Tallish» means a bit tall, and «greenish» means a bit green. When you meet a new word ending in -ish, take off the -ish, find the meaning of the base word, and then add «a bit» or «roughly» to it.
fact: Roundish means almost round, but not quite a perfect circle or ball.
fact: The ending -ish means a bit or roughly, so «tallish» means a bit tall.
fact: Roundish shapes are often found in nature, such as pebbles, seeds and leaves.
fact: Everyday roundish things include faces, buns and tables.
fact: For numbers, roundish means roughly a round number: 98 is roundish 100.
exercise: Ella says her pizza is roundish, not a perfect circle. What does roundish mean here? | Square with sharp corners | Long and thin like a stick | Perfectly round like a ball | *Almost round, but not a perfect circle
exercise: «The pebble was roundish, smooth and a little flat on one side.» What is the pebble like? | A flat square tile | A perfect sphere with no flat parts | A long thin stick | *Almost round, but not quite a perfect ball
exercise: «The crowd was 98 people, a roundish number.» Which round number is it close to? | 10 | 50 | *100 | 1000
test: «The seeds were roundish and brown, and some had tiny ridges.» Find and copy one word that means almost round. | *roundish | ridges | seeds | brown
test: Jayden says, «The bun was roundish.» What does he mean about the bun? | It was square with flat sides | It was long like a stick | *It was almost round, but not quite perfect | It was a perfect circle with no bumps
exam: «The leaves on the tree were roundish, not perfectly round.» What does roundish mean? | Square with straight edges | *Almost round | Long and pointy | Perfectly round like a coin
